{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":490926,"name":"looker dakidaki","username":"looker_dakidaki","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/67e7ee/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-14T14:43:55.328Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490926-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490926-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490926-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490926-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot is currently unusable on my account.\u003cbr\u003e\nMessages can be sent successfully in the chat UI, but multiple Bots give no response.\u003cbr\u003e\nMy Grok Bot Agent Computer has already been reset and appears reachable/connected. My local Windows computer is also connected. Usage/tokens are available, and Privacy Mode is Active.\u003cbr\u003e\nHowever, the Bot execution layer still appears stuck: messages are sent, but no reply is generated.\u003cbr\u003e\nPlease check whether the Grok Bot runner / Agent Computer associated with my account is stuck or in a partial backend state, and recover / reattach / reprovision it if necessary.\u003cbr\u003e\nPlease preserve my existing Bots, configurations, conversations, and Agent Computer data if possible.\u003cbr\u003e\nPlease do not ask me to repeatedly reset the Agent Computer. I have already completed a reset and the issue persists.\u003cbr\u003e\nCursor account email available privately to support if needed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490926-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490926-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOpen Grok Bot on Windows.\u003cbr\u003e\nOpen an existing Bot, for example my Chief of Staff Bot.\u003cbr\u003e\nSend a simple message such as “reply OK”.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe message appears normally in the chat.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe Bot never replies.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe same issue occurs with multiple Bots.Already tried:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAgent Computer reset\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFull app quit and reopen\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVerified local computer is connected\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVerified usage/tokens are available\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVerified Privacy Mode is Active\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRetried simple messages\u003cbr\u003e\nThe issue persists.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490926-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490926-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot should respond normally after I send a message and resume execution of existing Bot tasks.\u003cbr\u003e\nIf the Agent Computer or backend runner is stuck, I expect it to be recovered or reattached without deleting my existing Bots, configurations, conversations, or project data.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490926-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490926-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/4/b/4bbb059c796f8931348bf0a6b3cc9d5036736625.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/aNWvb8oYSxidsOjpV6auhyG9ESp.png?dl=1\" title=\"image.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/4/b/4bbb059c796f8931348bf0a6b3cc9d5036736625_2_687x500.png\" alt=\"image.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"aNWvb8oYSxidsOjpV6auhyG9ESp\" width=\"687\" height=